  "behavior": [
    "For Oblivion NIF versions20.0.0.4/20.0.0.5, scan complete reachable NiAVObject hierarchy before deciding whether a root has bhk collision. Keep all AV nodes in each physical hierarchy, including helpers and nonphysical branches, as dynamic record transforms so optimizers preserve author locals and distinct native world-cache identities. Identity roots cannot collapse to a generic Group. Existing billboard/type-specific construction remains; no new traversal policy for unsupported types is implied.",
    "Retain nativeNifRecordType and nativeNifFlags on these nodes as immutable source policy inputs. Flags retain full parsed uint32 storage and are not computed live NiAVObject update flags. OSG cloned userdata containers can share ValueObjects; callers must not mutate source metadata. The runtime owner must derive and own separate live flags.",
    "Tests load both supported versions with root/helper/physical-target/unrelated sibling, optimize with production-style permissions, clone twice with actual SceneUtil::CopyOp and rebind actual NifSceneTraversal. Every record remains a distinct MatrixTransform with its original translation/scale/type/flags. Only the first clone receives drawing handles and changes its world cache from106.75to206.75; source and second clone remain at6.75 without handles. Nonphysical Oblivion identity roots retain static Group optimization and have no physics metadata. Existing Morrowind control also passes."
  ],
